A||||19||Shaun41178||Raced a '00 Ford Lightning||||14||
Z||000000||Shaun41178||10-18-2000||12:35 AM||||Sat night out at the local hangout just chillin'.  Not much of a turn out and it is getting late around 1'ish.  So I leave and am driving down the cruising strip when I see a New Ford Lightning pickup.  I thought to myself that he won't race a Fiero so I slowly pass by and don't even give a rev at him.  Well as soon as I am about 2 cars ahead of him I hear him get on it and hear that supercharger whine.  Well he got me by surprise cause by the time my car reacted he was next to me and passing me.  He had the momentum and he pulled about 3-4 truck lengths on me before I shut down around 80 or so.<P>About a mile down the road I pull up next to him but couldn't see the guy as his truck was sitting too high but I jumped it full throttle and then let off and was about a car ahead of him when I heard that supercharger whine again but this time I was ready.  I nailed it from about 45 again and this time I held it up to 80 and he wasn't able to pull up next to me.  In fact I couldn't even see his bumper out my side window after I shutdown.  He flew by me as he stayed on it after I shutdown.  I was like Hell yea!!!  A Ford lightning having trouble pulling a Fiero!!  Well we raced one more time from a roll and he pulled 2 trucks on me slowly from 45-85.  I was happy as hell to have hung with a Lightning so well.  Sure he beat me but it wasn't that bad of a loss.  I wonder how well I would have done with a 90 shot instead of a 70 shot.<P>We pull into a Wendys and start talking.  He is all bragging how his truck is so fast and how he beats Ls'1's all the time.  He asked me how much hp I had and I told him 140.  HEHEHE  He then goes on to say that his has 360 hp and has run 13.9 at the track at 99 mph.  I then told him that I have run 14.1 at only 90.  He didn't seem too impressed because I think his head was so big from having a brand new Lightning and beating a Fiero no less.  It seemed like he didn't hear one word I said or cared really.  He just kept saying how he never loses and how even at lights he beats everyone off the line.  So I tell the guy that I will try him from a light.  He declined however.  Maybe because I kept insisting on going from a light instead of a roll.  Its too bad he didn't agree to go from a light cause I would have spanked him badly up to about 75-80 mph untill I hit OD.  Oh well.  Besides the big head, the guy was cool.<P>Man I can't wait for my 3.2 to go in.  Track that Lightning down and give him an @ss whoopin' like never before.  Street racing rules!! <P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||14
Z||000001||saleenfiero||10-18-2000||01:45 AM||||Kick ass win there.  Seems to me that anybody that buys a lightning for more than the rareness of the machine would have an ego massage from the get go.  Hell, I'd love one. Same seems to go for those old 199X chev 454SS's anybody in those act like they are unstoppable.  But a lightning beating an LS1 driven by a good driver?  Seems like a stretch.<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||11
Z||000002||BBBAD GT||10-18-2000||09:10 AM||||I'm not going to comment on street racing, but....<P>Want to know why the Lightning didn't want to race you again?  Its because <B>he had nothing to gain, and you had nothing to lose</B>.  I'm not flaming you personally, I just wanted to point out a common situation between two non-comparable cars and people's attitudes.  If I were to witness this race at a dragstrip, I would probably be thinking "this truck should beat this Fiero, if he doesn't, then something is wrong with the truck", when I should be saying "Man, that Fiero is fast, sure isn't stock, wonder what he's done to it."<P>Lets flip the coin here, lets say a Geo Metro pulled up next to a Fiero and they both went at it.  Of course, the Fiero wins.  Do you think the Fiero guy will be bragging that he beat a Metro?  But, do you think the Metro guy will post on his Metro BBS that he "kept up for a while".  In the Metro guys eyes, he won for keeping up.  So who gained and who didn't from this race?  <P>This is purely my opinions, hope I didn't upset anybody.<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||10-18-2000||09:38 AM||||Wow. Getting so philosophical BBBAD.  Sounds right.  I wouldn't waste the gas to let a "confirmed kill" get a second chance.  He'd only be hoping you miss a gear or make some other mistake so he can a win under his belt.   Maybe you get a pedestrian stuck under your front tire or through the windshield, that's bound to slow you down. he he. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||10-18-2000||10:51 AM||||nice pseudo-kill  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Shaun! he (lightning guy) like many street racer V8s have that i'm better than you mentality and will talk a big game but few pony up.. BBBAD has a SWEET @$$ mustang but has the street racing bug well under control. and not the swolen head like many others... can't WAIT till my car is driveable!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> we should hook up and go rail on over-weight V8 butt!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> hurry up and put your MOTOR TOGETHER!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shaun41178||10-18-2000||03:45 PM||||You are right BBad.  He didn't have anything to gain after beating me twice.  I just wanted to go from a light and see how I would have faired in that situation instead of from a roll.  My car does not do too well from a roll against known faster cars.  That is why I like to go from lights cause that is the strongest part of my car(Lightweight and good torque to launch hard).  I don't think the guy was a wuss either for not wanting to go from a light.  In fact it was probably the smart thing since we had run 3 times already with good luck and the 4th we might not have been so lucky and got caught.  Why push your luck too much right?<P>Oh yea I am not saying it was a kill by me it is just that I kept up better then I thought I would have.  After all he was pulling away from me 2 out of the 3 times.  More of an ego victory I guess.||||reg||7
Z||000006||Raydar||10-18-2000||05:42 PM||||Thas' alright. Sounds to me like you got his attention. And earned a bit of respect. Off the line, I think you woulda nailed him. And I think he probably thought the same thing. It takes an awful lot of steam to get something as big as a Lightning rolling. <BR>(Anchors aweigh!) <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||14
Z||000007||rockcrawl||10-18-2000||07:55 PM||||FWIW, The new Lightning is more suited to compete against a C5 Corvette than a Fiero. Hot Rod, May 2000, Corvette vs Lightning. The Vette's best time was 13.27 at 107MPH, the Ford ran 13.68 at 99.3MPH. Vette dynoed at 295.7 rwhp and 308.6 ft/lb. The Lightning 320.8rwhp and 410 ft/lb, which calculates to 385 Hp at the flywheel. If it wasn't for the trucks weight of 4250 lbs, Vette owners would have a serious problem on their hands. Be assured, that Lightning could beat your Fiero any way he wanted to, and he can also pick up a sheet of plywood on the way home!<P>I don't own a Lightning, but I do like ford trucks almost as muck as Fieros.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||10-18-2000||10:34 PM||||An SC 3800 (with modified blower pulley) powered Fiero should take them both. Run 222HP and 273ft-lbs at the wheels in a 3000lb (driver and gas inc.) Formula through a racing program and see.||||reg||1
Z||000009||BBBAD GT||10-18-2000||11:59 PM||||In one of my 'Ford' mags, they took a stock Lightning which ran high 13's stock and pulled 320 rwhp, and did two simple mods (80mm MAF and chip) and got 370 rwhp, which is well over 400 flywheel hp.  I know of a guy who specializes in Lightnings in NY, and is running low 12's at 110 mph with mostly stock parts (and lots of chip tuning).  They can run, but it is tough to get that 4700lb to 'get up and go'.||||reg||1
Z||000010||pollock||10-19-2000||10:38 AM||||There was a recent showdown article between a vette and a Lightning, can't remember which magazine.  they were pretty close.  <P>There was a bit of suspicion as to the "stockness" of the Lightning, as ford said, "here, use THIS one."<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||olympic||10-20-2000||12:38 AM||||  They are always talking about racing Lightnings over at LS1.com.  The LS1 usually wins but not by much.  Stock the lightning is a high 13/low 14's truck, the LS1 is a low 13's car.  So basically it will come down to the drivers.||||reg||1
Z||000012||gtsonly||10-22-2000||07:08 PM||||people, people please......................<BR>there has become a trend for some people on the forum to really stretch the truth about street racing. this maybe one of those times. A FORD LIGHTING with a SUPERCHARGER!!!<BR>am i the only one who thinks this is a stretch. a ford lighting with grannie driving back and forth to church everyday can wipe the streets against a fiero. the man driving the ford must not have wanted to waste the gas on a fiero. its like me wanting to race my gt against the kid down the street in the wheelchair. get it, handicapped!!!!!   just a few weeks ago there was a person bragging about racing a bmw z3 and blowing it off the road only after he broke the tires lose in 2nd and 3rd! yeah right!!!!!!!!!!!<BR> the fiero's are fun to drive and they do scoot down the street but please stop with the exaggerartions. the fiero is not the most prized auto among others and it is harder to save face with stories like these.<BR> my two cents!!<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||13
Z||000013||1FST2M6||10-23-2000||08:28 AM||||i'd be willin to say it's not a streach.. shauns car on nitrous will run 14.0 in the 1/4.. a lightin on street tires in street trim on a not so perfect street surface will be about the same due to our superior weight and weight distribution. a nice easy shot of nitrous will yeah not make 350hp.. but we don't need 350 to hang with that heavy truck. the math isn't that hard. 225hp in a 2600lb car or 350 in a 3700lb truck.. humm.. sounds pretty equal to me. check out shauns web page he's posted dyno results. my 86 would run 13.6@103 1/4, thats just as fast as a C4 or the lightning. and went through 16+ bottles of nitrous  with no motor destruction! even off nitorus i could chirp 4th at 80+ GT Bastard STILL does.. with no nitrous! so many people rant and rave cause their cars are slow compared to.. or i did this and i'm still slow... you need to research and tune your car to what you want. runin ONLY pump gas with proper tuning and DOT drag tires (Nitto NT555R 205-60-14) i was able to pilot my SE to 14.7in the 1/4 that was EASY... GT Bastard STILL wipes the floor with that car with a suiciding #5 rod bearing! Shaun said he hung with the truck he didn't kill it or get smoked by it.  <BR>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg">   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Shaun41178||10-23-2000||06:15 PM||||gtsonly:  I think you should read my whole post before giving us your opinion on how fast a Fiero is.  Yours is probably one of the many V6's that are stock or slightly modified with an ignition coil or something like that.  However mine is not.  If you read more closely I stated that I have Nitrous oxide on my Fiero and that I have also run a 14.1 qtr mile.  The Lightning owner told me that he has run a 13.9 qtr mile.  So thats only .2 seconds of a difference so you don't think that is close?  Thats only a few car lengths just like my original post stated.  I am not sporting attitude, I am just asking you to read more closely.<P>If you have time take a drive here to Toledo OH, I will show you how well my car hangs and beats many cars around here including Ford Lightnings.  I will be more then happy to give you a ride in the "Little Red Machine"  I might even have my 3.2 in by then and then you will really have to hold on.<P>Thanks Travis for covering my back there.  You know what it's like.<P><P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000015||sluppy123||10-23-2000||07:10 PM||||I'll agree with 1fst2m6. Having just installed Nitrous on my 87 GT I'd have to say shaun's telling the truth. Adding a extra 70-90 HP really helped my car out. Granted my car's not stock( but come to think of it everything in the engine compartment is Modified in one way or another)and even with an auto trans I can keep up with most of the cars on the street while on N2O. <P>And that's my .02<P>------------------<BR>-Brian S. <BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT-Leather, Lowered and On The Bottle||||reg||14
