Z||000019||Shaun41178||10-25-2000||01:01 PM||||A 40 nitrous jet is equivalant to about a 90 shot.  That is up there for sure.  I have only used a 40 jet at the track once and I was worried that it might not hold out.  it seemed to do ok but when one is 60 miles from home getting home is the bigger worry if something breaks.  But I did run my fastest time with a 90 shot although only by a tenth.    Funny thing is I ran a slower mph then with a 70 shot.  Hehe, weird stuff.  Stupid auto tranny.<P>If you see this Trav could you check out the nitrous post in the tech section.  got a couple of questions for you there.  thanks.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I love Whoop @ss Gas!!<P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
